      "value": "@{58c6cbcffd04b1785f747b6c|full_name}: This is not a practical workaround. It may sound similar to uploading your world to a different ID, then test it, change the ID and build + upload + test again (which takes a lot of time for large projects). This may work for small creators, but VRChat wants us to earn money now (the main income for some people) and any mistake we make directly affects our customers and our reputation. VRChat is no longer a hobby project for some creators and the tools should reflect that. \n\nEssentially creating a copy of your store in a private group to test things is not similar and sufficient, because you would still need to manually recreate all changes in the main version of your store afterward (where mistakes can be made), meanwhile, people will always see the \"work in progress\" version of your store in between all the changes because you are forced to work on the live version. But we want to make all the changes and push them live at once when everything is done and properly tested.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
